  "Muddy Makes a Square\n\nMuddy has six sticks in a tin. Muddy takes four sticks and makes a square. Two sticks stay in the tin. Pip asks for a big square. Muddy spreads the four sticks apart. The corners no longer meet. Pip brings four longer sticks for the bigger square.": "/audio/production/en-US/comprehension/f7cc8cdb8d887a8c6e69.mp3",
  "How many sticks does Muddy use for the first square?": "/audio/production/en-US/comprehension/ba6dfccce6a8cd899a07.mp3",
