  "Fluff Makes a Clay Print\n\nFluff presses a toy bone into soft clay. Fluff lifts the bone and sees its shape. Next, Fluff presses a stone close to the first print. The stone makes a round mark. Fluff leaves the clay flat on a shelf. The two prints stay as the clay dries.": "/audio/production/en-US/comprehension/aec1d89bd20eca34f68b.mp3",
  "What does Fluff press into the clay first?": "/audio/production/en-US/comprehension/29c62369090deed0b32d.mp3",
